# SecureDocs — .gitignore
#
# This repo is public and handles PII by design, so the secrets section comes
# first and is deliberately broad. Everything else is grouped by the tool that
# produces it, including tools from later roadmap phases so the rule exists
# before the artifact does.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Secrets and credentials — never commit these
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Environment files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.template

# Keys and certificates
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_ed25519
*.ppk

# cosign signing keys (Phase 3). The public key IS safe to commit — *.key
# does not match cosign.pub, so it stays tracked.
cosign.key
*.private.key

# Cloud credentials
.aws/
.azure/
credentials
*credentials.json
*service-account*.json
gcp-key*.json

# Plaintext / decrypted secret manifests.
# SOPS- or Sealed-Secrets-encrypted files are SAFE to commit and are re-included
# below — that is the whole point of committing them.
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
secrets.*.yaml
*.dec.yaml
*.dec.yml
*.decrypted.*
*.plain.yaml
!*sealed*.yaml
!*sealed*.yml
!*.sops.yaml
!*.sops.yml

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. Kubernetes
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Cluster credentials — a kubeconfig is a credential, not config
kubeconfig
kubeconfig.*
*.kubeconfig
.kube/

# Exported container images
*.tar
*.tar.gz

# Dumps captured while debugging
*-describe.txt
*-logs.txt

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. Helm
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Vendored subcharts pulled by `helm dependency update`.
# Chart.lock IS committed — it pins the versions, same role as a lockfile.
charts/**/charts/
**/charts/*.tgz
*.tgz

# Local value overrides that are not part of the delivered config
values.local.yaml
values-local.yaml
*.local.values.yaml

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. Terraform (Phase 2 — EKS/AKS)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl.bak

# State: contains every resource attribute in plaintext, including passwords
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info

# Plan files embed resolved values the same way state does.
# (AceArena has l0/tfplan and l1/tfplan committed — do not repeat that here.)
tfplan
*.tfplan
plan.out

crash.log
crash.*.log

# tfvars may carry secrets; commit an example instead
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!example.tfvars
!*.example.tfvars

override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# The provider lock file SHOULD be committed so the team pins identical versions
!.terraform.lock.hcl

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. .NET 9 (web / api / worker / migrator)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Ll]og/
[Ll]ogs/
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs
*.rsuser
TestResults/
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
*.coverage
*.coveragexml
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
project.lock.json
msbuild.log
msbuild.err
*.binlog

# Local-only app config. appsettings.json and appsettings.Development.json are
# committed by convention — keep real values out of them and use User Secrets
# or External Secrets Operator instead.
appsettings.Local.json
appsettings.*.local.json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 6. Node / Tailwind (Blazor front end)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

node_modules/
dist/
.npm
.yarn/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.pnpm-store/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 7. Security tooling output (Phases 3–4)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Scan reports are regenerated every run and go stale immediately
trivy-results.*
trivy-report.*
*.sarif
gitleaks-report.*
semgrep-results.*
checkov-report.*
kube-bench-*.json

# SBOMs — publish these as release artifacts / attestations, not repo files
sbom.json
sbom-*.json
*.spdx.json
*.cdx.json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 8. Tooling, editors, OS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Claude Code. settings.json currently holds machine-specific WSL paths, so the
# whole directory is ignored. If you later want to share project permissions
# with a collaborator, delete the first line and keep the .local.json rule —
# settings.local.json is personal and must always stay ignored.
.claude/
.claude/settings.local.json

.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 9. Personal notes — this repo is public and shown to employers
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# These are written *to me*, not to a reader of the repo. They contain career
# planning, target employers, and a skills audit that says "Kubernetes:
# Beginner" — the opposite of what a portfolio repo should say.
#
# README.md stays tracked: it is the public front door.
#
# When something here becomes genuinely public-worthy (an architecture doc, an
# ADR, a runbook, a postmortem), rewrite it for an outside reader and commit it
# under docs/ as a new file rather than un-ignoring one of these.

ROADMAP.md
LEARNING.md
PROJECT-DESIGN.md
docs/k8s-notes.md
docs/setup-log.md

# Local convenience scripts. They hardcode my machine's PATH ($HOME/.dotnet,
# $HOME/.local/bin) and exist to rebuild *my* laptop environment, not to be
# run by anyone else.
scripts/

# Convention for anything personal added later — keeps this list from growing
private/
notes/
*.private.md
*.local.md
*-notes.md
*-log.md

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 10. Scratch
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

tmp/
temp/
scratch/
.cache/
*.log
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej